# gradlew is a POSIX shell script; its line endings MUST be LF.
#
# Without this rule you hit a trap that is expensive to debug: a Windows checkout gives a CRLF gradlew,
# and running it under WSL/Linux reports
#     ./gradlew: cannot execute: required file not found
# which reads like "file not found". The real cause is a \r at the end of the shebang line, so the kernel
# looks for an interpreter called "/bin/sh\r". This has actually happened in a sibling repository.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# The wrapper jar is binary; any line-ending conversion corrupts it
gradle-wrapper.jar binary
